he first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours.\n\n","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,7824,315,279,444,324,352,356,33718,82,304,12989,6786,30161,1449,220,17,15,4420,13,8886,1899,304,5813,279,1156,7216,374,518,220,24,264,744,2572,323,279,1537,7216,8471,518,220,21,281,744,13,2585,1657,30161,525,1052,817,1899,304,5813,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198,1249,8253,279,1372,315,30161,13075,817,1899,518,279,444,324,352,356,33718,82,304,5813,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,28301,1437,279,2790,1372,315,4115,279,30161,14476,1817,1899,25,1019,256,481,576,1156,7216,8471,518,220,24,264,744,624,256,481,576,1537,7216,8471,518,220,21,281,744,624,256,481,576,2790,10350,882,374,504,220,24,264,744,13,311,220,21,281,744,2572,892,374,220,24,4115,382],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe owners of the Luray Caverns in Virginia conduct tours every 20 minutes. Each day in April the first tour is at 9 a.m., and the last tour starts at 6 p.m. How many tours are there per day in April?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"d31eb9a970664a8ddb915b58703a29adb0ed0ddd6a589657051de14c182efcb7"},"seconds":14.714323282241821,"seed":848218633426243484,"stop":"eos","text":"2. **Convert the operating time into minutes:**\n   - 9 hours = 9 × 60 = 540 minutes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of tours conducted within the operating time:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - To find the number of tours, divide the total operating time in minutes by the interval between tours:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{540 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ minutes per tour}} = 27 \\text{ tours}\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, let's consider the timing of the tours:\n- The first tour starts at 9:00 a.m.\n- The second tour starts at 9:20 a.m.\n- The third tour starts at 9:40 a.m.\n- This pattern continues every 20 minutes until the last tour at 6:00 p.m.\n\nSince the tours start every 20 minutes and the last tour starts exactly at 6:00 p.m., the count is correct.\n\nTherefore, the number of tours per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":true},"graded_text":"To determine the number of tours conducted per day at the Luray Caverns in April, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Identify the total number of hours the tours operate each day:**\n   - The first tour starts at 9 a.m.\n   - The last tour starts at 6 p.m.\n   - The total operating time is from 9 a.m. to 6 p.m., which is 9 hours.\n\n2. **Convert the operating time into minutes:**\n   - 9 hours = 9 × 60 = 540 minutes.\n\n3. **Calculate the number of tours conducted within the operating time:**\n   - Tours are conducted every 20 minutes.\n   - To find the number of tours, divide the total operating time in minutes by the interval between tours:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{540 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ minutes per tour}} = 27 \\text{ tours}\n     \\]\n\nTo verify, let's consider the timing of the tours:\n- The first tour starts at 9:00 a.m.\n- The second tour starts at 9:20 a.m.\n- The third tour starts at 9:40 a.m.\n- This pattern continues every 20 minutes until the last tour at 6:00 p.m.\n\nSince the tours start every 20 minutes and the last tour starts exactly at 6:00 p.m., the count is correct.\n\nTherefore, the number of tours per day in April is \\(\\boxed{27}\\).","id":"algebra:932"}
